</example><div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="623e7202-5ef2-49ad-8752-b3e9f0039917" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0" data-wait-for-event="RFM1">
  <exercise data-content-id="e9f36468-a618-4a55-b863-9bf452b3b22c" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="12">
    <problem>
      <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
      <para>There are two more Platonic solids: an octahedron, which has 8 faces that are all triangles, and an
        icosahedron, which has 20 faces that are all triangles.</para>
      <para>How many edges would each of these solids have? (Keep in mind that each edge is used in two faces.)</para>
      <para>The octahedron has how many edges? </para>
      <para> Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para> Correct! The octahedron has 12 edges.</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="ea62c583-6289-4dca-904c-a02e8d2aa5a4" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="30">
    <problem>
      <para>The icosahedron has how many edges? </para>
      <para> Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para> Correct! The icosahedron has 30 edges.</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="b87cc191-53ed-4e73-b056-a9786c8409a7" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="6">
    <problem>
      <para>Use your discoveries from the activity to determine how many vertices each of these solids would have.</para>
      <para>The octahedron has how many vertices? </para>
      <para> Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para> Correct! The octahedron has 6 vertices.</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="7a2261b6-0c6f-4594-99b2-7534849eed92" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="30">
    <problem>
      <para>The icosahedron has how many vertices? </para>
      <para> Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para> Correct! The icosahedron has 30 vertices.</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  </div>
<exercise data-wait-for-event="RFM1">
  <problem>
    <para>For all 5 Platonic solids, determine how many faces meet at each vertex.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The tetrahedron, cube, and dodecahedron have 3 faces meeting at each vertex. The octahedron has 4 faces meeting
      at each vertex. The icosahedron has 5 faces meeting at each vertex.</para>
  </solution></exercise></section>
